#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""KimLogPipe v2 - one event schema for system logs, threshold rules, live follow.

No AI, no model and no network. All data stays inside
$XDG_DATA_HOME/kimlogpipe/ (fallback ~/.local/share/kimlogpipe/).

Two modes:

* one-shot - ``ingest`` reads a fixture or a snapshot, ``detect`` evaluates the
  rules, ``report`` prints a human summary.
* live - ``follow`` keeps reading ``journalctl -f`` and the audit log, writes
  events as they arrive and pushes new findings to KimAI over its Unix socket.
  If KimAI is down the pipeline keeps running in tools-only mode.

The event schema is deliberately small and uniform so every finding can be
traced back to a raw log line:

    {"ts","source","host","user","src_ip","action","outcome","raw_ref","path"}
"""

